unities\nWellness\nBuilding Community\nAccommodations and Academic Considerations\nCounselling and Advising Services\nCampus Resources\nFamily Resources\nResources for Distance & Online Learners\nProfessional Development\nHow it Works\nWorkshops & Events\nProfessional Development Plan\nPhD-Community Initiative\nOverview\nCurrent Projects\nPast Projects\nQueen's Public Scholarship Program\nOverview\nWriting Camps\nInternships\nInternship Opportunities\nQDIUA\nOnline Courses\nCampus Resources\nFaculty & Staff\nSupervision and Support\nSupporting Student Wellness\nAdmission and Registration\nDegree Completion\nCourse-based Masters\nMaster\u2019s Oral Thesis Examination\nDoctoral Oral Thesis Examination\nExternal Examiners\nRecruiting a Postdoc\nProgram Changes & Quality Assurance\nAcademic Calendar(s)\nForms\nContact Us\nSGSPA Office Contacts\nProgram Contacts\nHave a Question?\nLead the Way\nHere at the SGSPA, we believe learning is inspired by an inclusive and collaborative community where we prioritize wellbeing for academic and professional success. Through our local and global reach, we connect our graduate students and fellows with diverse communities to engage in collaborative knowledge creation and real world scholarship. Our graduate students and postdoctoral fellows lead the way toward a better future for our global community. Learn more about our mission, vision, and values.\nPrograms and Degrees\nAcademic Calendar\nProfessional Development\nWellness and Inclusivity\nQueen's Special U.S. Doctoral Recruitment Initiative\nYou Belong Here\nApply to Queen\u2019s as a graduate student or postdoctoral fellow\nTALK to a Current Graduate Student about Queen's Life and Graduate Studies\nQueen\u2019s University continues its tradition of excellence in graduate education by warmly welcoming a dynamic 2026-27 cohort of domestic and international graduate students. To support students, graduate programs that provide a minimum funding guarantee for graduate students are maintaining or increasing these commitments in 2026-27. These incoming students will be central to Queen\u2019s ongoing innovations in research, teaching, and community engagement, contributing to a thriving graduate community in which they shape our academic mission towards a better future for all.\nSpotlights\nNational awards celebrate achievements in physics and law\nBhavin Shastri and Raquel Medeiros are among 41 recipients of the Royal Society of Canada\u2019s 2026 awards.\nQueen's Gazette\nThree Queen's researchers elected to the Royal Society of Canada\nThree Queen\u2019s researchers will join the Royal Society of Canada (RSC), bringing expertise in operations research, exercise science, and educational assessment.\nQueen's Gazette\nUpcoming Events\nDissertation Day Camp\nOctober 26, 2026 at 9:00 am to October 26, 2026 at 4:00 pm\nPA Day Writing Circle\nOctober 26, 2026 at 9:00 am to October 26, 2026 at 4:00 pm\nFunding Your Graduate Education at Queen's\nOctober 28, 2026 at 12:00 pm to October 28, 2026 at 1:00 pm\nGraduate Studies and Postdoctoral Affairs\nQueen's University\n74 Union Street\nKingston, ON K7L 3N6\nCanada\nPhone: 1-613-533-6100\nContact Us\nGradifying Blog\nFooter Menu 3\nDonate to SGSPA\nWeb Privacy\nQueen\u2019s University is situated on the territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabek.\n\u00a9 2026 Queen\u2019s University", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.queensu.ca/grad-postdoc/#main-content"], ["Skip to footer", "https://www.queensu.ca/grad-postdoc/#footer"], ["", "https://www.queensu.ca/"], ["Sign In", "https://www.queensu.ca/grad-postdoc/"], ["", "https://www.queensu.ca/grad-postdoc/"], ["School of Graduate Studies and Postdoctoral Affairs", "https://www.queensu.ca/grad-postdoc/"], ["Home", "https://www.queensu.ca/grad-postdoc/"], ["About Down arrow", "https://www.queensu.ca/grad-postdoc/"], ["Welcome", "https://www.queensu.ca/grad-postdoc/about/welcome"], ["Mission, Vision, & Values", "https://www.queensu.ca/grad-pos